// YeTerm —— English translations
//
// Format:  "<Chinese source>" = "<English>";
// The Chinese text IS the key. Anything missing here simply falls back to
// Chinese, so a partial translation is always safe to ship.
//
// Placeholders (%@, %d, %1$@ …) must be preserved exactly, including their
// order numbers — those are how the value gets substituted back in.
//
// To add another language: copy this file to <code>.strings (e.g. ja.strings),
// translate the right-hand side, and add the case to AppLanguage in
// Sources/YeTermKit/Config/Localization.swift.

